      "text": [
        " «وَ مَا اَلْمَلاَّحَةُ» فَقُلْتُ أَرْضٌ سَبِخَةٌ مَالِحَةٌ يَجْتَمِعُ فِيهَا اَلْمَاءُ فَيَصِيرُ مِلْحاً فَقَالَ «مِثْلُ اَلْمَعْدِنِ فِيهِ اَلْخُمُسُ» قُلْتُ فَالْكِبْرِيتُ وَ اَلنِّفْطُ يُخْرَجُ مِنَ اَلْأَرْضِ فَقَالَ «هَذَا وَ أَشْبَاهُهُ فِيهِ اَلْخُمُسُ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1648 - Muhammad ibn Muslim asked Abu Ja’far Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as) about salt flats.\nThe Imam asked: \"What are salt flats?\"\nI replied: \"They are salty, barren lands where water collects and turns into salt.\"\nThe Imam (as) said: \"It is like a mine; Khums is due on it.\"\nI asked: \"What about sulfur and oil extracted from the earth?\"\nImam (as) replied: \"These and similar things also require Khums.\""
        ]
      }
